			"Message": "chore(Land): Update OXC toolchain to 0.128.0 and sync Element with defensive hardening\n\nBump OXC dependencies from 0.127.0 to 0.128.0 across allocator, parser, transformer, minifier, codegen, semantic, span, and ast. Also update supporting crates: open (5.3.4), rustls (0.23.40), rustls-pki-types (1.14.1), zip (8.6.0).\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to d1fcac15, bringing Mountain's centralized LogSkyEmit for histogram visibility across 7 provider files, defensive URI/path guards in DiagnosticProvider/PathSecurity/FileSystem, and terminal resilience improvements. Sky receives defensive try/catch wrappers around all Tauri listener handlers to isolate failures rather than crash the listener loop.",
			"SHA": "40fe64f579addc5a8c4b70b5f914b033e3eaeaf1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:52:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates completing extensions race fix\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (2b89f60a): Fix boot-time extensions race and add missing getLatency handler. Add polling to extensions:getInstalled to resolve race condition where workbench caches empty extension list before ExtensionPopulate completes its scan (~250-500ms). Poll ScannedExtensions map for up to 3 seconds before returning empty, ensuring 113+ extension contributions appear in activity bar. Also add localPty:getLatency handler returning empty array per VS Code's IPtyHostLatencyMeasurement[] contract, eliminating \"Unknown IPC command\" log noise.\n- Output (1f47ba96): Correct ViewContainersRegistry registry ID in ViewRegistrySnapshot diagnostic. The function was using guessed ID 'workbench.view.containersRegistry' which returned null. Fix uses correct stock VS Code registry ID 'workbench.registry.view.containers' from vs/workbench/common/views.ts, enabling SkyBridge diagnostics to correctly report extension view counts.\n- Cocoon (92c434cd): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nThis synchronization completes the extensions race fix cycle and restores diagnostic visibility for extension view registration.",
			"SHA": "91fceb68b2aab07d1282a84dbabb667dcc899bee"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:42:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync Element submodules with upstream fixes\n\nSynchronize the Element submodule to caa2b47f, bringing multiple downstream updates:\n- Mountain: Fix duplicate DevTools window in debug builds by removing redundant open_devtools() call from WindowBuild.rs, update DiagnosticProvider docstring to clarify 1-based indexing\n- Output: Disable PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration transform due to \"black shadow over text\" artifacts in WKWebView, add ViewRegistrySnapshot() to __CEL_SERVICES__ facade\n- Sky: Add reentrancy guard (_SkyBridgeInstalled, _SkyBridgeInstallPromise) to prevent duplicate Tauri listen() registrations causing double-render \"purple overlays\" bug, update astro.config.ts with static output and disabled prerendering\n- Cocoon: Submodule sync bringing cross-cutting synchronizations\n\nThis synchronization brings in the reentrancy guard fix for the workbench loading twice issue, disables the GPU acceleration transform that introduced visual artifacts, and removes the duplicate DevTools window opening behavior.",
			"SHA": "02d2e32fffdabcfccc45d1d45b5e13040d5f0800"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
